# BRAND SYSTEM
The website represents a premium enterprise managed IT and cybersecurity company.
The visual identity should communicate:
- trust
- competence
- technical sophistication
- security
- reliability
- maturity
- precision
- premium service
The website should NOT feel:
- childish
- gimmicky
- cyberpunk
- hacker-themed
- overly futuristic
- generic SaaS
- AI-generated
- stock-photo driven
- visually noisy
# VISUAL LANGUAGE
The core visual direction is:
PREMIUM ENTERPRISE TECHNOLOGY
+
DARK TECHNICAL ENVIRONMENT
+
RESTRAINED VIOLET ACCENTS
+
SOPHISTICATED 3D / DIGITAL VISUALIZATION
Think high-end enterprise technology product visualization rather than generic cybersecurity artwork.
## COLOR
Primary environment:
- near black `#0a0a0a`
- charcoal `#151217`
- graphite `--de-bg` `#050312` / `--de-surface` `#0a0714`
- dark gray
Accent:
- deep violet `#5B45E0` / `#7c3aed`
- restrained purple `#8B5CF6`
- subtle lavender `#A78BFA`
- brand magenta `#D3126A` (primary CTA, brand mark, active glow)
Purple should primarily function as an accent or source of illumination.
Avoid large areas of saturated neon purple.
Avoid rainbow gradients.
Avoid excessive bright white.
## MATERIALS
Preferred:
- graphite
- gunmetal
- smoked glass
- dark metal
- subtle translucent materials
- controlled reflective surfaces
Avoid:
- toy-like plastic
- excessive chrome
- cheap glossy surfaces
- cartoon materials
## LIGHTING
Preferred:
- controlled studio lighting
- subtle rim lighting
- soft violet illumination
- deep shadows
- restrained highlights
- cinematic but clean lighting
Avoid:
- blown-out highlights
- excessive bloom
- giant neon glows
- cyberpunk lighting
- rainbow lighting
## TYPOGRAPHY
Typography should feel:
- modern
- highly legible
- confident
- restrained
- professional
Use hierarchy intentionally.
Do not compensate for weak hierarchy by making everything larger or bolder.
Live type: Space Grotesk (headings), Inter (body), Oxanium / JetBrains Mono (stats).
## CARDS
Cards should feel like part of a coherent interface.
Avoid:
- excessive floating cards
- excessive rounded containers
- random card treatments
- inconsistent border radii
- inconsistent padding
Prefer:
- consistent spacing
- subtle borders
- controlled contrast
- clear hierarchy
- strong internal composition
## IMAGERY
Do not automatically represent concepts literally.
Avoid default imagery such as:
- shield for cybersecurity
- padlock for security
- laptop for IT
- robot for AI/IT
- hacker in hoodie
- generic server rack
- glowing binary code
Instead communicate the underlying concept.
Example:
Managed IT:
centralized infrastructure and orchestration
Co-managed IT:
two complementary systems working together
Risk assessment:
infrastructure being analyzed/scanned
Monitoring:
technical telemetry and system state
Identity:
controlled access architecture
Backup:
redundancy and layered infrastructure
## DESIGN PRINCIPLE
Every visual element should have a reason to exist.
When choosing between:
"more visual effects"
and
"better composition"
choose better composition.
When choosing between:
"more decoration"
and
"better hierarchy"
choose better hierarchy.
Premium design should feel intentional, not busy.
